  "scope": "Recorded proposal activation on captured live input only, not host execution or strength. 65 boards from eight live 6p Continents Online games of 11-15/16 that lost the original capital (civvis-20261115T222126Z Rome t110-116, -20261116T033254Z Rome t133-143, -20261115T095713Z Athens t113-123, -20261115T125708Z Athens t89-95, -20261116T032213Z Athens t87-90, -20261116T032722Z Uruk t87-90, -20261115T204822Z Uruk t60-72, -20261115T142213Z St. Petersburg t197-204), each the run's events.jsonl cut after turn N+1 and replayed at turn N. Both arms run one frozen release civvis_orders --resumed built from the branch at 3e78397647 with the run's own requested genome (why.log line 1 forced); the on arm adds --with spared-soldiers-come-to-the-capital. Off arms journal 122 Anvil one-blow rewrites at the capital to tiles four or more out; on arms 44 (soldiers holding another city of ours, which the gene leaves alone) and 95 'comes in to' lines. Orders differ on 18 of 65 boards; over the 65, land soldiers more than two tiles from the capital ordered to move nearer it rise from 58 to 84 and holds fall from 62 to 54. The Rome boards of 033254Z form no Anvil on the replayed frame (live did, on a later frame), and 032722Z's Anvil spares nobody: both read identical, as they should.",
